values ('f4a5b6c7-8d9e-4f64-9a34-4b5c6d7e8f64', 'u-s-foreign-policy', 'U.S. Foreign Policy', 'This course examines how the United States defines interests, chooses strategies, builds institutions, deploys power, and responds to global change. Students study the historical development of U.S. foreign policy, the institutions and domestic forces that shape decisions, major regional and functional challenges, and the professional craft of policy analysis. The course combines historical cases, theory, current strategy documents, and applied memo writing so students can explain past choices and produce practical recommendations for contemporary problems.');

